From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topazio Mobile Server OS <topazio@0xtpz.org>
Date: 2026-10-04
Subject: [PATCH] sea: bq2589x: use a strict no-argument prototype

The pinned Xiaomi tree exports get_charger_type() and declares its consumer
as get_charger_type(void). Clang r433403b promotes the old-style definition
to an error because the charger directory enables -Werror. This localized
prototype correction preserves the exported ABI and charging behavior.

Evidence: Mission 007 reproduction at
drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c:117, and the matching
extern declaration in mtk_chg_type_det.c:562.

Topazio patch metadata:
  ID: TPZ-M007-002
  File: drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c
  Problem: -Wstrict-prototypes under Clang/Werror
  Category: C_ACTUAL_SOURCE_BUG; E_CRITICAL_SUBSYSTEM
  Justification: a prototype-only correction; no charging logic changes
  Source/evidence: pinned Xiaomi sea-t-oss source and Mission 007 log
  Impact: restores compilation of the BQ2589x charging driver
  Risk: low; exported function type already matches all consumers
  Subsystem: power/charging
  Reversibility: remove this patch

---
 drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/bq2589x_charger.c
@@ -117,1 +117,1 @@
-int get_charger_type()
+int get_charger_type(void)
-- 
2.39.0
